Lab 33: Basic Web Scraping with requests + BeautifulSoup
Objectives

Understand the basics of web scraping using requests and BeautifulSoup.

Learn how to retrieve web pages and parse HTML content.

Extract specific pieces of information from a webpage.

Prerequisites

Basic knowledge of Python programming.

Python installed on your system.

Familiarity with HTML basics will be beneficial.

Lab Tasks
Task 1: Setup Your Environment
1.1 Install Required Python Packages

To perform web scraping, install BeautifulSoup and requests using the following command:

pip install beautifulsoup4 requests

Note: Ensure your Python environment is active and has internet access.

1.2 Verify the Installation
pip show beautifulsoup4 requests

Check the installed version numbers to verify successful installations.

Task 2: Fetch a Webpage
2.1 Use requests to Get a Webpage
import requests


# Send a GET request to the webpage
response = requests.get("https://example.com")


# Print the status code of the response
print(response.status_code)

A status code of 200 indicates that the request was successful.

Task 3: Parse the HTML Content
3.1 Parse with BeautifulSoup
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup


# Parse the HTML content
soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, 'html.parser')


# Display the structured format of the parsed content
print(soup.prettify())

BeautifulSoup is used to parse and navigate HTML content. The html.parser is built-in and sufficient for basic scraping tasks.

Task 4: Extract Specific Information
4.1 Extract the Page Title
# Extract and print the page title
title = soup.title.string
print("Page Title:", title)

The page title provides a brief description of the webpage content.

4.2 Extract All Hyperlinks (<a> tags)
# Find all hyperlinks on the page
links = soup.find_all('a')


# Loop through each link and print the hyperlink reference
for link in links:
    print(link.get('href'))

The get('href') method retrieves the URLs from anchor tags.

Key Concepts

HTTP Requests: Using requests to fetch web content.

HTML Parsing: Utilizing BeautifulSoup to parse HTML documents.

DOM Navigation: Extracting data by navigating HTML tags.

Conclusion

In this lab, you learned the basics of web scraping using Python’s requests and BeautifulSoup libraries. You practiced fetching a webpage, parsing HTML content, and extracting elements such as titles and hyperlinks. These foundational skills prepare you for more advanced web scraping tasks.

Happy Scraping! 🕷️
